                "text_H9iLx6": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Diamond color measures the absence of color, with colorless diamonds being the most valuable and rare. The GIA scale ranges from D (colorless) to Z, with each grade indicating a subtle increase in color saturation. Diamonds outside this range, like vivid pinks or blues, are classified as \"fancy colored.\"</p><p></p><p>Color becomes more noticeable in larger diamonds, making it crucial for larger selections. When choosing a diamond, consider factors like mounting style (yellow gold can enhance the whiteness of near-colorless diamonds), diamond size (larger stones reveal more color), and shape (step-cuts tend to show more color than brilliant cuts).</p>",
